ut when  you break it down there are basically  three reasons you'd want a Dynomax the  first is to do big damage max moves are  super powerful and in the hands of a  strong attacker like Durant they can  one-hit ko Pokemon if your opponent  isn't prepared the second is to trigger  stat changes whether or Terrain max worm  wind reduces your opponent's attack  while max Starfall triggers misty Tyrion  for example and the third is to increase  your overall bulkiness Dynomax thing is  the only thing that can increase your  total HP in a battle and it can make  defensive pokémon like melodic even  harder to take down at a pinch you can  do all of these things at once - Durant  is an incredible Dynomax candidate  because of its sheer power and speed and  also its move pool this one knows steel  rock and ground type moves max rock fall  will trigger a sandstorm if needed while  max steel spike boosts your defense and  max quake boost special defense  this helps Durant lived through its  three Dynomax turns in tandem with the  HP boost although during special defense  is pretty bad so it's better to knock  out special attackers the stat boosts  also really helped Durant's partner as  the battle wears on by making it harder  to take down that's just one example of  a good Dynomax choice and it's  definitely a mechanic that will shift  over time the best way to really get a  sense of good Dynomax strategies and  battle strategies in general is to just  practice you'll see what other people  are doing and you'll figure out over  time what does and doesn't work about  the team's you use  [Music]  while battling online you will often  have the chance to view your opponent's  team after the battle which I highly  recommend this can expose you to items  abilities or moves you didn't know about  as well as the kinds of sets people run  on certain Pokemon I also really  recommend using rental teams made by  experienced players so you can start  battling right away getting experience  and then moving on to breeding which is  why breeding and training is the next  video you can find great rental teams on  Victory Road VGC and trainer tower  sometimes with full breakdowns and  explanations by the team's creator as  always please reach out to me in the  comments or on Twitter with any  questions stay tuned for the next video  all about breeding and training and  thanks for watching  [Music]
 

